[[File:KingGnu2025.jpg|175px|thumb|upright|[[King Gnu]] dominated the chart in 2025, with their massive hit "Abyssal" holding the number one spot for four consecutive weeks in April and May, becoming the best-performing single of the year. Hip-hop acts like [[Creepy Nuts]], [[Awich]], and [[Lana (singer)|LANA]] also saw multiple weeks at number one, cementing the dominance of the genre.]]

The '''PYRAMID30 Okaiken''' is a chart that ranks the best-performing singles in [[Okaiken]]. Its data, published by Nikkan Sports & Entertainment magazine, KTK Group and compiled by Okaiken Pyramid Records, is based collectively on each single's weekly physical and digital sales, as well as radio airplay and streaming. PYRAMID30 Okaiken is a subsidiary of Pyramid Records but acts as a separate organization. The weekly charts are updated every Sunday at 11:45 in the morning (UTC +9). The following lists all of the number one singles of the PYRAMID30 Okaiken for 2025.

In 2025, the Okaiken music scene was characterized by the continued dominance of domestic hip-hop, particularly the "Sanese Drill" subgenre, and a resurgence of stadium rock. International collaborations were also prominent, with Western artists featuring on several chart-topping tracks.

